#55100
Chapter Four - Faerie Dwellings~
   As far as fairy-human relationships are concerned, the operative word is
caution.  Dont forget that fairies are magical creatures, and very proud.  We
may invite them into our world, but we can never force them to stay.  If they
feel that they are coerced, or that you are prying into their private lives,
they are likely to turn very aggressive or leave you altogether.  In fact, it
is a great compliment to be visited by fairies.  It means you are one of the
Good People, because Bad People never see fairies!  We can only be grateful
when they give us a glimpse into their whimsical world.    
~
551 520 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
~
~
0 0 55198
D3
~
~
0 0 55194
S
#55101
A Strange Circle~
   The ring consist of mushrooms and rocks in a circle.  In its center is what
resembles a very ancient and tattered book.  As you approch you have a feeling
as if someone is watching you, but you see no one there, a feeling as if an
insect is touching you when it appears that there isn't one there, a wonderful
fragrance fills the air, and hushed giggling comes from behind you, or was it
in front of you?  In the distant glowing objects float in the shadows.  
Fireflies maybe?    
~
551 32772 0 0 0 3 255 0
D2
~
~
0 0 30586
S
#55102
The Book of Faeries - Introduction~
   Faerie is a world of dark enchantment, of captivating beauty, of enormous
ugliness, of callous superficiality, of humor, mischief, joy and inspiration,
of terror, laughter, love and tragedy.  It is far richer than fiction would
generally lead one to believe and, beyond that, it is a world to enter with
extreme caution, for of all things that faeries resent the most it is curious
humans blundering about their private domains like so many ill-mannered
tourists.  So go softly, where the rewards are enchanting, the dangers real.  
~
