#55108
Chapter Two - Hollow Hills~
   Ancient earthworks, forts and barrows are the traditional home of faeries.
The Gaelic for faerie is Sidhe, meaning people of the hills.  At night faerie
hills are often seen ablaze with myriad sparkling lights.  Sometimes the Hill
may rise itself up on pillars to reveal the brilliant lights of Faerie which
gradually move off in procession towards another hill.    
~
