Chapter Four - Faerie Dwellings~
   Fairies belong to all peoples of the world.  That is, all cultures share the
idea that trees and plants, flowers and herbs and mushrooms are the dwelling
places of tiny creatures, not supernatural beings, but very natural, born of
the earth and its earthy energies.  From Eastern plant divas to Irish
leprechauns, from the gnomes and elves of Middle Earth to Snow Whites dwarfs
and our own childhood pixies, fairies have lived and played in human
imagination for many centuries.    
~
