#55192
Chapter Four - Faerie Dwellings~
   In folklore, a fairy is a creature who looks mostly like one of us,except
that he or she is tiny.  Some fairies live in fairyland, a place that is, long
ago and far away.  In some imaginings, fairyland is a magical, perfect world,
where the fairies never grow old and nothing bad ever happens.  In other
imaginings, it is a world like our own, that is, there are good fairies and bad
fairies, and changing times and seasons, except that it is entirely magical.  
However fairyland is imagined, though, it is never ordinary.  It is always
quite extraordinary with fanciful forests and mountains, cottages and castles.
  
~
