#55193
Chapter Four - Faerie Dwellings~
   But there is another, more homely imagining of fairyland, as close to us as
our own gardens and woodlands and fields.  This is the fairyland you may have
visited when you were a child, when you could (if you listened) hear the
chiming of the blue bells, and the elves came at night to feast on your mothers
ripest strawberries, and pixies wore sweet pea bonnets and ladies slippers and
soft-as-velvet foxgloves.  This is the delightful fairyland we can come back to
time and again, even as adults, because entering it requires only a turn of the
heart and an opening of the imagination.  In this garden fairyland (which might
be a tiny collection of miniature fairy-pleasing plants on your windowsill), we
are once again children at heart, and our garden play is healthy and healing.
All we have to do is look around us with a childs believing eyes, and see the
charmed truths of fairies.    
~
