Chapter Four - Faerie Dwellings~
   There are, trooping fairies who live in families and clans and like nothing
better than dancing fairy reels in fairy rings in the moonlight, and solitary
fairies (perhaps a more sober and industrious lot) who live by themselves and
dont get along with other fairies very well.  I imagine that solitary fairies
have too much to do to spend time dancing, they have large herb gardens to tend
and thimbles-full of fairy potpourri to make.  Of course, there are men fairies
and lady fairies, which leads (naturally) to baby girl and boy fairies, who
swing in rosemary cradles.  There are grandmother and grandfather fairies who
might be very old, but then again, might not.  Past a certain age, fairy years
become rather indeterminant.    
~
