   We might also describe fairies in terms of where they like to live.  There
are garden fairies and woodland fairies, most imagine that woodland fairies are
the wilder sort, and garden fairies more kindly toward humans.  There are marsh
fairies, some of these can be quite daunting, and stream fairies.  Perhaps
there are even city fairies, too, who are charmed by visits to the zoo and
evenings at the opera and who find their most natural home in the exuberant
flower gardens of the park or in exotic blooms in florists windows.  (Next time
you walk by such a shop, see if you can spy one!  )
